  {
   "id": "bava_batra.60a.11",
   "daf": "60a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "אֵין מוֹצִיאִין זִיזִין וּגְזוּזְטְרָאוֹת וְכוּ׳. רַבִּי אַמֵּי הֲוָה לֵיהּ זִיזָא דַּהֲוָה נָפֵיק לִמְבוֹאָה; וְהַהוּא גַּבְרָא נָמֵי הֲוָה לֵיהּ זִיזָא, דַּהֲוָה מַפֵּיק לִרְשׁוּת הָרַבִּים. הֲווֹ קָא מְעַכְּבִי עֲלֵיהּ בְּנֵי רְשׁוּת הָרַבִּים. אֲתָא לְקַמֵּיהּ דְּרַבִּי אַמֵּי, אֲמַר לֵיהּ: זִיל קוֹץ.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches that «one may not extend projections or balconies» into the public domain. The Gemara relates: «Rabbi Ami had a projection that protruded into an alleyway, and a certain man also had a projection that protruded into the public domain,» and the «general public was preventing» the man from leaving it there, as it interfered with traffic. He «came before Rabbi Ami,» who «said to him: Go sever» your projection."
  }
 ],
